// How Typst builds its own reference documentation
// =================================================
//
// A summary of findings from reading the `typst` repository, written up as a
// design reference for building Twyla's own reference docs. Twyla already uses
// the typst crates internally, so most of this machinery is reusable.
//
// TL;DR: Typst does NOT use rustdoc/Markdown. It compiles its reference *as a
// Typst document*. Stdlib metadata (including the `///` doc comments) is scraped
// at compile time by attribute macros, baked into the binary, and then exposed
// back to Typst markup through a small reflection API. The doc comments
// themselves are Typst markup, evaluated with `eval(.., mode: "markup")`.

